Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 696.1969 cm
q
.090196 .168627 .227451 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 42.8 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 13 TL (This project demonstrates private IPv4 communication between two separate AWS VPCs by using VPC Peering. The) Tj T* (implementation combines non-overlapping CIDR ranges, subnet design, route-table entries in both directions, and) Tj T* (scoped security-group rules. App-A and App-B were tested from their private EC2 shells, without public IPv4) Tj T* (addresses on either application instance.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 651.1969 cm
q
.090196 .168627 .227451 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 29.8 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 13 TL (A controlled negative test removed the relevant inbound ICMP Echo Request rule on App-B. Ping from App-A then) Tj T* (showed 100% packet loss. Restoring the rule returned the test to four replies with 0% packet loss. This shows how a) Tj T* (security-group rule can control the tested traffic path.) Tj T* ET
